{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1115588-masquerade-revenants-in-requiem","id":1115588,"title":"masquerade revenants in Requiem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-13T10:48:30-07:00","id":1115588,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> masquerade revenants in Requiem","content":"So I really love the Revenants of Masquerade, them being sort of super ghouls that don't need a regnant, and i know that Requiems Revenants are nothing like that. So the Question is is there anything in Vampire the Requiem like that, or would i have to home brew it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T11:04:08-07:00","id":1115600,"title":"","content":"Ghoul families are similar but need a regent. Half Dammed is expected to go into rules for dampires (half vampire half human) but isn't out yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T11:17:51-07:00","id":1115604,"title":"","content":"There might be something in Mythologies or the upcoming Half-Damned, but as far as I know you would have to home brew it.<br /> <br /> It shouldn't be hard, really, they're just natural born ghouls who age slowly and create their own Vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T17:39:09-07:00","id":1115726,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Ghoul families cover the niche, and they'll be getting an update in Half-Damned. You might take a look at the older <b>Ghouls</b> supplement if you want to mine ideas without waiting. Basically, as of first edition, Ghoul family members age 2 years for every 3 they exist, and don't revert to their true ages when they're cut off from vampire blood. They also have mechanical strengths and weaknesses. There might be other factors I'm not remembering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T21:20:41-07:00","id":1115781,"title":"","content":"As others said, you'll have to homebrew it for now around ghoul families. These have a lineage that gives them an hereditary discipline, boon and bane. Below is a homebrew version I've adapted for use based on the initial work of a few posters on these forums--I've since forgotten names, but they might recognize part of it. (Sorry!)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Hereditary Ghoul (Variable Merit)</b><br /> An odd quirk of the blood, Ghoul &quot;families&quot; are a phenomena that arises every so often where a Ghoul's condition becomes hereditary. While these family lines aren't always the most stable, usually dying out or dispersing after a few generations, a small number of lineages do manage to survive due to either luck or a Kindred hand.<br /> <br /> The following benefits are in addition to the benefits of being a Ghoul.<br /> <b>Blood Ties: </b>A Hereditary Ghoul does not require the expenditure of a willpower point during feeding, its body is already adapted to the blood and absorbs it with no effort.<br /> <b>Aging:</b> A Hereditary Ghoul ages only two years for every three they actually live. This aging is paused when they become a Ghoul by having vitae within them, as usual.<br /> <b>Hereditary Disciplines:</b> Some lineages pass certain Disciplines down through their blood; Ghouls of that family line may take a dot in any of those Disciplines as one of their starting Disciplines, in addition to the Clan Disciplines of their Regent.<br /> <b>Bred Blood:</b> the Hereditary Ghoul merit is passed on through children; the offspring of such a ghoul has a base 25% chance to inherit a single dot of the merit, increased 5% per dot held by each parent. Subsequent dots may be inherited as well at the same percentage chance per dot. Even if a given child does not inherit the merit, he continues to carry a 5% base chance for it manifesting in grandchildren.<br /> <b>Vitae Tolerance:</b> A Hereditary Ghoul is born with a trace of Vitae in their system; while they still age when Deprived of Vitae, they age at their normal rate (see Aging, above) rather than one year per week. They also may take additional dots in the Hereditary Ghoul merit at Storyteller discretion.<br /> <b>Kindred Sense:</b> All Hereditary Ghouls receive Unseen Senses (Kindred) for free.<br /> <b>Lineage Boon and Bane:</b> Each &quot;dynasty&quot; has a Boon and a Bane; a Ghoul of that lineage automatically gains both. When exactly the Boon and Bane develop varies based on the Ghoul; in some cases, they showed signs prior to becoming a Ghoul. In other cases, the Ghoul in question might not develop them until up to a year after first being affected.<br /> <br /> <b>Hereditary Ghoul [Supernatural, Style; \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022]</b><br /> <i>Prerequisite</i>: Must be a Ghoul, must have been born into a Ghoul Family or acquired the Ghoul Family condition. Unlike most Ghouls, you were literally <i>born</i> this way; as such, your body has developed a high tolerance to Vitae, and your biology has become strange and twisted.<br /> <br /> <i>Born to the All-Night Society (\u2022)</i>: When you grow up around blood-drinking monsters, you tend to have a strong stomach. You never need to make Composure, Stamina, or Resolve rolls to resist the biologically strange, and you never suffer Breaking Points due to observing the supernatural abilities of Ghouls or Kindred.<br /> <br /> <i>Filling the Tanks (\u2022\u2022)</i>: You have grown used to holding Vitae; add your dots in this Merit to your Stamina for the purposes of determining your maximum Vitae. However, &quot;used to&quot; doesn't mean &quot;happy with&quot;; you feel bloated and slightly nauseous as long as you have more Vitae in your pool than your actual Stamina, preventing you from regaining Willpower through rest.<br /> <br /> <i>Vitae Symbiosis (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i>: The Vitae in your veins is as natural as the blood it uses as a medium; unlike other Ghouls, the cycle doesn't leak <i>nearly</i> as much. You only have to spend Vitae once per year to remain a Ghoul, rather than once per month. In addition, you may reflexively spend one Willpower to increase your spending limit for Vitae by one for that turn.<br /> <br /> <i>The Blood is the Life</i> <i>(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i>: Your body already knows how to convert Vitae into flesh and blood. More worryingly, it has learned to work the other way around. You may choose to take 1 level of Lethal damage whenever you would recover Willpower through rest; doing so allows you to gain one Vitae.<br /> <br /> <i>Adoptive Vitae (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i>: The Vitae you produce naturally has similar supernatural qualities to kindred blood. You may feed another Ghoul one Vitae and spend one Willpower <i>dot</i> to adopt that Ghoul into the family, giving them all the inherent benefits and drawbacks of being &quot;part of the family&quot;. If the Ghoul in question is pregnant, they may adopt their unborn child as if they were a Ghoul.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Please note that the 5th dot above is <i><b>extremely powerful</b></i>. Being able to adopt members into a ghoul family should be very rare and would make the holder incredibly valuable. Holding the 4th dot essentially makes them the same as a Masquerade revenant--an extremely useful and durable servant, or an implacable foe.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}]